Subject: [PATCH 22/25] feat(theme): GATE 6a visual diff tooling + fix navy
 sidebar/navbar cascade loss
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds scripts/visual-diff.mjs (Playwright + pixelmatch) and VERIFY.md per
GATE 6's automated/manual split. Running it against a live dev server
surfaced a real bug: Fuselage's dynamically-inserted #sidebar-palette
style tag (dark-mode PaletteStyleTag) was winning the cascade over
eprisi-tokens.css on tied selector specificity, so the navbar/sidebar
rendered Fuselage's gray instead of the Eprisi navy — exactly the risk
GATE 2's own comment had flagged as unverified. Fixed by doubling
selector specificity (.rcx-navbar.rcx-navbar etc.), verified via
computed style against the live app.

Also logs several open, non-CSS findings (missing font-family utility
on shadcn form controls, unbranded login logo/copy, no hero-image slot
for the login aside) as deferred items in .visual/report.json rather
than expanding this gate's scope to fix them inline.
