+# GATE 6b — Manual Visual Verification
+
+This is the human half of GATE 6 (see `REDESIGN_PROMPT.md`). GATE 6a's automated
+pass (`scripts/visual-diff.mjs`) already produced `.visual/report.json` with
+screenshots, pixel diffs, and a structured list of findings — read that first.
+This checklist is for opening the live app in **Claude in Chrome** (or your own
+browser) and checking things a pixel diff can't: hover/focus states,
+interaction flows, and subjective "does this feel right" judgment.
+
+## Environment
+
+- App: `http://localhost:3000` (Meteor dev server, `yarn dev` in `apps/meteor`)
+- Test admin: `eprisiadmin` / `EprisiVerify14#Ok`
+- This is a local air-gapped dev instance seeded only for this verification —
+  not a real workspace. One channel exists: `#general`.
+- If the dev server isn't running: prepend the pinned Node toolchain
+  (`.toolchain/node-v22.22.3-darwin-arm64/bin`) and Meteor
+  (`~/.meteor`) to `PATH`, ensure the `rc-eprisi-mongo` Docker container is
+  running (`docker start rc-eprisi-mongo` if stopped), then `yarn dev` in
+  `apps/meteor`.
+
+## Known gaps (don't re-report these — see `.visual/report.json` for detail)
+
+- Login logo/copy still shows stock Rocket.Chat branding, not the mockup's
+  "EPRISI Chat" wordmark — content/asset gap, not a CSS bug.
+- Login aside has no hero photo/marketing copy — no settings slot exists for
+  that in Rocket.Chat today.
+- Shadcn Button/Input render in the browser's default control font instead of
+  IBM Plex Sans (computed `font-family: Arial`) — traced to a missing
+  Tailwind font utility from GATE 3, open for a fix decision.
+- Sidebar channel rows show a colored avatar tile instead of the mockup's
+  plain "#" hash icon — toggleable via the existing `sidebarDisplayAvatar`
+  setting, not a defect.
+- No multi-workspace icon rail (mockup shows one) — Rocket.Chat has no
+  multi-workspace concept, reported as a gap in GATE 5.
+
+## Screens and steps
+
+### 1. Login (`http://localhost:3000/`, logged out)
+
+- [ ] Brand color: primary button fill matches `#3E5C8A` (Eprisi brand-600)
+- [ ] Input fields use the light blue-gray tint (`#E8EEF5`), not stock white/gray
+- [ ] Radius: buttons and inputs have visibly rounded corners (~6-10px), not RC's stock sharp/minimal radius
+- [ ] Body copy renders in a humanist sans (IBM Plex Sans) — compare letterforms against system default; note if it looks like a fallback font instead (see known gap above)
+- [ ] Heading ("Login") renders in a distinct, bolder display face (Plus Jakarta Sans) vs. the body text font
+- [ ] Hover state: hovering the primary "Login" button visibly darkens/changes it
+- [ ] Focus state: Tab to the email field — a visible focus ring appears (brand-colored, not browser default blue)
+- [ ] Error state: submit with a wrong password — an inline error message appears below the field in a legible color (not clipped/overlapping)
+- [ ] "Forgot your password?" link is legible and brand-colored
+- [ ] Responsive: resize to ~390px wide (or use the mobile emulator) — form remains usable, no horizontal scroll, aside panel stacks or hides sensibly
+
+### 2. Register (`http://localhost:3000/register` if registration is enabled, or via "New here?")
+
+- [ ] Same brand color/radius/font checks as Login
+- [ ] Required-field validation shows inline errors on submit with empty fields
+- [ ] Password strength/requirements text is legible against the input background
+
+### 3. Reset password (via "Forgot your password?")
+
+- [ ] Same brand color/radius/font checks
+- [ ] Success state after submitting a valid email is clearly communicated (not just a silent redirect)
+
+### 4. Home dashboard (`http://localhost:3000/home`, logged in as `eprisiadmin`)
+
+- [ ] Navbar background is dark navy (`#0A2535`), not gray — **this was a real
+      bug found and fixed during GATE 6a (Fuselage's dynamic dark-mode style
+      tag was overriding it); re-confirm it still holds after any further
+      changes**
+- [ ] Sidebar background is dark navy (`#0F1728`), distinct from the navbar's shade
+- [ ] Search bar in the navbar reads as a dark pill with light placeholder text, not a plain white input
+- [ ] Click into `#general`: the sidebar row shows a rounded blue pill (brand-600) with white text, not the default RC gray/blue
+- [ ] Hover over an unselected sidebar row: subtle lighter highlight appears
+- [ ] Icons in the navbar (bell, gear, back/forward, avatar menu) are light-colored/visible against the dark background, not dark-on-dark
+- [ ] Dark mode: if you have OS-level dark mode, or use Chrome DevTools to force `prefers-color-scheme: dark` — confirm the navbar/sidebar don't visually break (this fork intentionally did not touch dark mode; the light-theme navy sidebar and RC's real dark theme happen to be visually close, but check for jarring transitions)
+- [ ] Responsive: resize to ~390px wide — sidebar collapses to a hamburger menu, no layout breakage, search bar still reachable
+
+### 5. Functional checks (not visual, but quick to verify while you're in there)
+
+- [ ] Login succeeds with `eprisiadmin` / `EprisiVerify14#Ok`
+- [ ] Login fails gracefully with a wrong password (error shown, no crash)
+- [ ] Registration form appears/works if `Accounts_RegistrationForm` is enabled (currently likely disabled — not required for GATE 6, note if you toggle it)
+- [ ] OAuth/SSO buttons: none configured in this dev instance, so none should appear — this matches the login screen showing no "Login with Eprisi Account" button (that's a mockup-only concept until an OAuth provider is actually configured)
+- [ ] Custom logo from admin panel: Admin → Layout → Assets lets you upload a
+      custom logo; if you upload one, confirm it appears in place of the
+      Rocket.Chat wordmark on both the login screen and navbar — this is the
+      real mechanism for closing the branding gap noted above
+
+## When done
+
+Note any checklist item that fails in the chat/PR, referencing this file. If
+everything passes except the already-known gaps above, GATE 6 is clear to
+close.
